# HMR & LIVE GAME STATE SAFETY – CRITICAL

The user is frequently play-testing the dice game live. Full page reloads destroy progress, skins, and debugging state. Treat this as a high-priority constraint.

## Core Rules
1. Prefer the smallest change that can hot-reload without a full page refresh.
2. Never restart the Vite dev server or kill the process unless the user explicitly asks.
3. When editing game logic, scenes, or sprite *references*, structure the change so Vite can do a module hot update instead of a full reload whenever possible.
4. If a change will force a full page reload, **stop and warn the user first**. Offer a safer alternative if one exists.
5. After any change, clearly state whether it should hot-reload or will cause a full refresh.

## Phaser-specific (if applicable)
- Always destroy the old Phaser.Game instance cleanly on HMR using `import.meta.hot`.
- Use a singleton pattern or module-level `let game` + `import.meta.hot.dispose(() => game.destroy(true))`.
- Prefer updating config, scene data, or texture references over recreating the whole game when possible.

## Pixi / Canvas / Three.js
- Destroy the old Application / renderer / scene graph on HMR dispose.
- Clear any leftover canvas elements from the DOM before creating a new one.
- Keep asset loading and texture caches intact across hot updates when feasible.

## Asset / Skin Changes
- Never overwrite existing sprite sheets, texture atlases, or skin image files.
- Only change the code that points to them (paths, frame names, animation keys).
- If a new visual variant is needed, create a *new* file instead of modifying the original.

## When the user reports “it refreshed and reset” or “my skins disappeared”
- Immediately investigate whether the last change forced a full reload or overwrote an asset.
- Fix the root cause (HMR cleanup, asset overwrite, etc.) before continuing with other work.
